title: 'statement-store: keep blocking store calls off the async runtime'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Statement store calls that wait for the disk run on blocking threads: the validation workers,
    the gossip handler, the maintenance task and both RPC submit methods. The gossip loop reads the
    admission watermark from an atomic counter. Together these tasks could hold every worker
    thread of the runtime, so a collator under statement overload received blocks late and missed
    its authoring slots.
    Nodes that build the statement handler themselves should spawn the handler and its validation
    executor with `spawn_blocking`.
crates:
- name: sc-statement-store
  bump: patch
- name: sc-rpc-api
  bump: patch
- name: sc-rpc-spec-v2
  bump: patch
- name: polkadot-omni-node-lib
  bump: patch
- name: staging-node-cli
  bump: patch
